1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,991
Choosing sports gear means balancing price, suitability and what you already own.

2
00:00:04,991 --> 00:00:10,229
I built this personal project to connect those decisions: an evidence-backed shopping

3
00:00:10,229 --> 00:00:14,296
assistant, interactive planning tools and a responsive storefront.

4
00:00:14,296 --> 00:00:17,192
Let’s use the actual application, step by step.

5
00:00:17,792 --> 00:00:21,864
First, I ask about returns and delivery in one message.

6
00:00:21,864 --> 00:00:27,789
The assistant separates the questions and retrieves the relevant project guides.

7
00:00:27,789 --> 00:00:30,010
Notice the numbered citations.

8
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:36,008
I open a source to read the supporting policy, so the explanation can be checked.

9
00:00:36,008 --> 00:00:41,192
These are the demo store’s policies, not a promise about a real order.

10
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:44,072
Next, I compare badminton rackets.

11
00:00:44,072 --> 00:00:49,237
Catalogue fields power the side-by-side prices, materials and specifications.

12
00:00:49,237 --> 00:00:52,188
Missing information remains visibly missing.

13
00:00:52,188 --> 00:00:55,676
I open the BR 100 product page, then return to chat.

14
00:00:55,676 --> 00:00:57,823
The conversation is still there.

15
00:00:57,823 --> 00:01:02,317
Product exploration does not require starting the discussion again.

16
00:01:02,917 --> 00:01:06,032
For more guidance, I start a badminton kit.

17
00:01:06,032 --> 00:01:11,465
I choose an easy-to-handle racket, beginner experience and occasional play.

18
00:01:11,465 --> 00:01:17,188
The advisor turns those choices into a shared shopping brief, then explains its

19
00:01:17,188 --> 00:01:18,275
recommendation.

20
00:01:18,275 --> 00:01:24,578
The same pattern supports yoga pants, mats, backpacks and running shoes, with questions

21
00:01:24,578 --> 00:01:26,317
suited to each category.

22
00:01:26,917 --> 00:01:30,043
The Adjust tab makes recommendations interactive.

23
00:01:30,043 --> 00:01:31,957
I prioritise the lowest price.

24
00:01:31,957 --> 00:01:37,316
Here, the same racket still wins, and the app says so instead of inventing a change.

25
00:01:37,316 --> 00:01:39,421
Undo restores the previous brief.

26
00:01:39,421 --> 00:01:42,483
The comparison and kit use the same preferences.

27
00:01:43,083 --> 00:01:44,304
Now I build the kit.

28
00:01:44,304 --> 00:01:48,209
Each category asks whether I own it, need it or want to skip it.

29
00:01:48,209 --> 00:01:51,931
I mark court shoes as already owned and the racket as needed.

30
00:01:51,931 --> 00:01:57,483
New spending only includes the items I choose, with size selection required where relevant.

31
00:01:58,083 --> 00:02:02,160
Gear lab connects eight decision tools to one activity brief.

32
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:08,309
Compare starter and next-step kits, test expected conditions, narrow choices and track owned

33
00:02:08,309 --> 00:02:08,643
gear.

34
00:02:08,643 --> 00:02:13,121
Evidence tables distinguish requirements, preferences and unknowns.

35
00:02:13,121 --> 00:02:15,527
Team kits share suitable items once.

36
00:02:15,527 --> 00:02:17,933
Buy less suggests reuse or deferral.

37
00:02:17,933 --> 00:02:21,476
Community feedback is opt-in; empty data stays empty.

38
00:02:21,476 --> 00:02:24,483
Conditions are assumptions, not live weather.

39
00:02:25,083 --> 00:02:29,228
On mobile, the training plan becomes two focused views.

40
00:02:29,228 --> 00:02:34,276
I choose a sport, timing and budget, then mark the racket as owned.

41
00:02:34,276 --> 00:02:38,647
The total falls because it is excluded from new purchases.

42
00:02:38,647 --> 00:02:41,887
I open the weekly plan and expand week two.

43
00:02:41,887 --> 00:02:46,483
This is a gear purchase timeline, not a workout prescription.

44
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:51,620
The adventure planner connects preparation with shopping.

45
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:56,555
I choose yoga and a budget, reuse my mat, then build the plan.

46
00:02:56,555 --> 00:03:02,206
A checklist tracks preparation while the kit uses real catalogue items.

47
00:03:02,206 --> 00:03:04,832
Checking a task updates progress.

48
00:03:04,832 --> 00:03:10,483
I save the adventure on this device, ready to reopen or download later.

49
00:03:11,083 --> 00:03:15,344
Before committing to equipment, I can plan a first session.

50
00:03:15,344 --> 00:03:19,822
I enter a city, choose a session length and set a sample date.

51
00:03:19,822 --> 00:03:21,917
The suggested agenda updates.

52
00:03:21,917 --> 00:03:26,250
I save the personal plan; calendar export is also available.

53
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:29,644
After a real session, I can record how it felt.

54
00:03:29,644 --> 00:03:31,378
Venue search opens Maps.

55
00:03:31,378 --> 00:03:34,483
Saving does not book a court or instructor.

56
00:03:35,083 --> 00:03:39,655
Fit memories record the size and comfort someone actually experienced.

57
00:03:39,655 --> 00:03:45,206
For this demonstration, I enter clearly labelled sample feedback and consent to local

58
00:03:45,206 --> 00:03:45,728
storage.

59
00:03:45,728 --> 00:03:49,843
After saving, the exact same product offers my remembered size.

60
00:03:49,843 --> 00:03:51,279
I apply it explicitly.

61
00:03:51,279 --> 00:03:57,157
This is personal recall, not a body measurement or a guarantee that other products fit the

62
00:03:57,157 --> 00:03:57,483
same.

63
00:03:58,083 --> 00:04:01,902
The fitting room offers a live camera preview for supported tops.

64
00:04:01,902 --> 00:04:05,074
I change the garment and open the adjustment controls.

65
00:04:05,074 --> 00:04:09,833
A person with shoulders and waist visible is needed to demonstrate live tracking.

66
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,771
This chapter shows controls only.

67
00:04:11,771 --> 00:04:14,650
A visual overlay does not establish physical fit.

68
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:19,224
Finally, I select a size and add the racket to the shared cart.

69
00:04:19,224 --> 00:04:22,441
The price summary separates discounts and shipping.

70
00:04:22,441 --> 00:04:25,974
Checkout offers a simulated wallet and cash on delivery.

71
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:29,696
This portfolio demonstration stops before placing an order.

72
00:04:29,696 --> 00:04:31,525
No real payment is processed.

73
00:04:32,125 --> 00:04:37,742
Underneath, hybrid lexical retrieval, query expansion, rank fusion, guide context and

74
00:04:37,742 --> 00:04:40,914
conservative claim checks support the assistant.

75
00:04:40,914 --> 00:04:43,425
Optional model integrations extend it.

76
00:04:43,425 --> 00:04:49,109
The value is the connected journey: understand, compare, try, remember and plan before

77
00:04:49,109 --> 00:04:49,571
buying.

78
00:04:49,571 --> 00:04:52,942
Explore the source and documented limits on GitHub.
